216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 136 0 R
/E (Our project is based on the card game "Concentration" \(also known as "Memory"\). In the game, the first player is chosen by any method. The player then selects two cards to flip over, leaving the first card face up until the second card is revealed. If the two cards form a matching pair, the player takes them and places them face down in a pile, then turns over two more cards. If the cards do not form a pair, the player must wait for at least five seconds before turning them face down again, keeping them in their original positions on the table. The turn then passes to the next player \(usually the player to the left\). The game continues in this manner until all the cards are matched.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 136 0 R
/E (The idea for our project came about one day during our games period in class, when we were playing "Concentration" and having a great time. When we were later assigned to create a GUI project, we immediately thought of this game. We realized it would be both a fun and challenging project, so we decided to pursue it and quickly shared our idea with our teacher, who supported the plan.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
