221 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (After playing memory games like "Concentration," students often experience improved recall of specific names, terms, and functions. These games require concentration, pattern recognition, and attention to detail, all of which stimulate cognitive processes. Engaging in such activities not only enhances memory retention but also boosts overall brain function and activity. Studies have shown that memory games help strengthen neural connections, particularly in areas related to short-term and long-term memory. As a result, students become better at recalling information quickly and accurately, which can have a positive impact on their learning abilities across various subjects.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
222 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (In addition to improving memory, these games also foster critical thinking skills, as players must analyze patterns and make strategic decisions. The mental challenge involved in matching cards strengthens cognitive flexibility and problem-solving abilities, which are essential skills both in and outside of the classroom. By engaging with games like "Concentration," students develop a fun yet effective way to enhance their cognitive abilities, all while honing skills that will benefit them in academic and real-world situations.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
